  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Stonex Financial obligated $922M in FY2026 to date under federal contracts. Stonex Financial won 276 awards so far this fiscal year, and Stonex Financial average award size is $3.3M. Stonex Financial obligations are down 30.7% year over year. Stonex Financial fiscal-year obligations show the following history: FY21 was $1.1B, FY22 was $1.7B, FY23 was $1.7B, FY24 was $703M, FY25 was $1.3B, and FY26 is $922M to date. Stonex Financial current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing. Stonex Financial year-to-date figures reflect lower obligation activity versus the prior year while prior fiscal years include multiple years with higher obligation totals than FY26 to date. Stonex Financial award count and average award size signal transaction-level activity even as aggregate obligations declined for the current fiscal period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Stonex Financial obligations changed across fiscal years?",
        "body": "Stonex Financial obligations were $1.1B in FY21, rose to $1.7B in FY22 and remained $1.7B in FY23. Stonex Financial obligations fell to $703M in FY24, increased to $1.3B in FY25, and are $922M in FY26 to date. Stonex Financial obligations are down 30.7% year over year for FY26 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What do FY2026 figures reveal about Stonex Financial's current federal activity?",
        "body": "Stonex Financial obligated $922M in FY26 to date through 276 awards with an average award size of $3.3M. Stonex Financial totals for FY26 are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing. Stonex Financial year-over-year decline of 30.7% indicates reduced obligation flow in the current fiscal period."
      }
    ]
